-- title:
--   Ordinary eigenvectors dying under reduction span at most a line
-- statement:
--   Let $M\ge 1$ and let $g$ be a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_0(M)$ that is a newform in the project's sense: $g$ is a normalised eigenform and for every divisor $M'\mid M$ with $M'\neq M$ there is no normalised eigenform of weight two on $\Gamma_0(M')$ whose $q$-coefficients at all primes $\ell\nmid M$ agree with those of $g$. Let $\lambda$ be a prime with $\lambda\nmid M$, let $S$ be a finite set of naturals, and let $\mathcal O'$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for its maximal ideal, with finite residue field and with $\lambda$ in its maximal ideal. Let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism from the weight-two level-$M$ Hecke algebra away from $S\setminus\{\lambda\}$ (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of the cusp forms generated by the $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell\nmid M$, $\ell\notin S\setminus\{\lambda\}$, and the $U_q$ for primes $q\mid M$, $q\notin S\setminus\{\lambda\}$) to $\mathbb C$ with $\chi_g(T_\ell)=a_\ell(g)$ for all such $\ell$, and let $\iota$ be a ring homomorphism from the range of $\chi_g$ to $\mathcal O'$ such that $\iota(\chi_g(T_\lambda))$ is a unit. Let $\mathcal O''$ be a further characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation domain with finite residue field, module-finite over $\mathcal O'$ by a local algebra map and a $\mathbb Z_\lambda$-algebra, and let $K$ be a fraction field of $\mathcal O''$. Equip $J_0(M)=\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the modular function field of level $M$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with the Hecke action [`ModularCurve.heckeModuleBar`](def/ModularCurve_HeckeModule.html#L82), and let $T$ be its $\lambda$-adic Tate module, the Hecke-stable module of sequences $(x_n)$ in $J_0(M)$ with $x_0=0$ and $\lambda\cdot x_{n+1}=x_n$. The assertion is then: for every $\mathbb Z_\lambda$-module structure on $T$ whose scalar action is computed level-wise through the reduction $\mathbb Z_\lambda\to\mathbb Z/\lambda^n$, every ring homomorphism $TM$ from $\mathrm{HeckeAlg}=\mathbb Z[X_q:q\ \text{prime}]$ to $\operatorname{End}_{\mathcal O''}(\mathcal O''\otimes_{\mathbb Z_\lambda}T)$ acting on pure tensors by $a\otimes x\mapsto a\otimes (t\cdot x)$, every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\lambda$ a non-unit of $A$, and every $K$-submodule $U$ of $K\otimes_{\mathcal O''}(\mathcal O''\otimes_{\mathbb Z_\lambda}T)$ such that (i) for each prime $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\notin S$ the base change of $TM(X_\ell)$ acts on $U$ as the scalar image in $K$ of $\iota(\chi_g(T_\ell))$, (ii) the same holds at $\ell=\lambda$ for $T_\lambda$, and (iii) $U$ lies in the $K$-span of the image of $\{x\in T:\ \text{reduction mod }\mathfrak m_A\ \text{of}\ x_n\ \text{vanishes for all }n\}$ under $x\mapsto 1\otimes(1\otimes x)$, one has $\dim_K U\le 1$.
--
--   This is the connected half of Deligne's description of the local behaviour at $\lambda$ of the Galois representation attached to a $\lambda$-ordinary weight-two newform of level prime to $\lambda$, formulated inside the Tate module of the modular Jacobian: the $g$-eigenvectors killed by reduction at a place above $\lambda$ form at most a line. It is used by [`CuspForm.IsNewform.exists_specialization_jZeroOrdConn_eigenPlane_tateModule_jZero_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.IsNewform.exists_specialization_jZeroOrdConn_eigenPlane_tateModule_jZero_of_not_dvd) and [`CuspForm.IsNewform.frobenius_quadratic_mem_of_inertia_sub_mem_eigenPlane_tateModule_jZero_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.IsNewform.frobenius_quadratic_mem_of_inertia_sub_mem_eigenPlane_tateModule_jZero_of_not_dvd) in the analysis of the ordinary local condition at $\lambda$.
